<http://data.silknow.org/object/8880f985-3a85-3f6e-8757-41debc7ee07c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "One side of a pair of slippers for a man (most likely Han) made of woven and plaited straw for its vamp and sole, and which also has a layer of leather stitched at its bottom. It is unpadded and has a red silk tassel attached to the end of the heel."@en , "One side of a pair of slippers made of woven and plaited straw, China, 19th century"@en ;
